  "title": "Effective information of a network",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "10ac26ce-b8ea-4314-b790-097a34d39438",
      "text": "For a network, effective information is the entropy of the average out-weight distribution minus the average entropy of each node’s out-weights, the latter being the noise in the network’s relationships.",
